//? Title: Sign and Wilcoxon signed-rank tests for paired measurements
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Simulate measurements before and after an intervention on the same subjects.
An improvement increases the recorded response. Both tests use the pairing
and ask whether changes tend to be positive. The plot marks equality.
)

> Simulate, test and plot

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/paired_location.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace sp = dm::stats;
using dm::graphics::RPlot;

int main() {
    dm::set_seed(19);
    const auto before = dm::rnorm(12, 2.5, 28);
    const dm::Vector<> after = before + dm::rnorm(0.8, 1.3, before.size());
    const auto sign = sp::paired_sign_test(after, before, sp::Alternative::Greater);
    const auto ranks = sp::wilcoxon_paired_test(after, before, sp::Alternative::Greater);
    std::print("| Method | Statistic | p-value |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto* test : {&sign, &ranks})
        std::print("| {} | {:.1f} | {:.4g} |\n", test->method, test->statistic, test->p_value);
    std::print("\nPositive changes: {:.0f} of {:.0f} nonzero differences.\n",
               sign.statistic, sign.parameter1);

    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    RPlot::create().points(before, after, "subjects", {36, 105, 172})
        .abline(0, 1).title("Paired measurements").x_label("Before").y_label("After")
        .save_svg("build/paired_location.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| Method | Statistic | p-value |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Paired exact sign test | 20.0 | 0.01785 |
| Wilcoxon signed rank test (exact conditional sign flips) | 289.0 | 0.02525 |

Positive changes: 20 of 28 nonzero differences.
\image(figures/paired_location.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Each point is one subject. Points above the identity line improved.)
\alttext(Each point is one subject. Points above the identity line improved.)

> Interpretation

The sign test uses only the direction of each nonzero difference and has
an exact binomial reference. The signed-rank test also uses the ranks of their
absolute sizes. Its location interpretation assumes symmetric differences,
and this sample uses the exact conditional sign-flip reference. The paired API
switches to the tie- and continuity-corrected normal approximation above 100
nonzero differences.

> References

- [R Wilcoxon rank tests|https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/wilcox.test.html]
- [R exact binomial test|https://stat.ethz.ch/R-manual/R-devel/library/stats/html/binom.test.html]
